# YOUR OWN BUTTONS.
#
#   python3 -m parts run my-buttons.parts
#
# The window becomes a strip across the top and eight squares.
# Press one and it tells you which. Change the words in quotes
# to whatever you like -- the squares are yours.
#
# Only works in Termux itself, where the screen can be touched.

pad
banner "press a square"
button 1 "find files"
button 2 "spin a cube"
button 3 "paint"
button 4 "big files"
button 5 "my notes"
button 6 "downloads"
button 7 "more"
button 8 "back"
press
say "you pressed"
